      "text": "```\nPENICILLINS:\n  Natural: penicillin G (IV), V (PO) — Strep, syphilis, Clostridium\n  Antistaphylococcal (penicillinase-resistant): oxacillin/nafcillin/dicloxacillin\n    → Block penicillinase active site; bulky side chain prevents hydrolysis\n    → Active vs MSSA (NOT MRSA)\n  Aminopenicillins: ampicillin/amoxicillin — ↑ gram-neg spectrum (H. flu, E. coli, Listeria)\n  Ureidopenicillins: piperacillin-tazobactam (pip/tazo) — anti-pseudomonal + anaerobes"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-ANTIBIOTICS.md#014",
      "path": [
        "01-ANTIBIOTICS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:medicine:01-antibiotics, git-history:medicine:01-antibiotics]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/01-ANTIBIOTICS.md",
        "concepts": "[antibiotics]",
        "current_path": "medicine/01-ANTIBIOTICS.md",
        "id": "maxim:medicine:antibiotics",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[antibiotics]",
        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "01 - Antibiotics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "CEPHALOSPORINS (gen 1–5):\n  Gen 1 (cefazolin/cefalexin): gram+ cocci (MSSA, Strep); surgical prophylaxis\n  Gen 2 (cefuroxime/cefoxitin): ↑ gram-neg; cefoxitin has anaerobic (B. fragilis) coverage\n  Gen 3 (ceftriaxone/cefotaxime/ceftazidime): CSF penetration; ceftazidime = anti-Pseudomonas\n  Gen 4 (cefepime): anti-Pseudomonas + gram+; Enterobacteriaceae; \"Pseudomonas gen 3\"\n  Gen 5 (ceftaroline): MRSA coverage; anti-PBP2a; used for MRSA pneumonia/skin\n  Ceftolozane-tazobactam / ceftazidime-avibactam: ESBL + some carbapenem-resistant Enterobacterales"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-ANTIBIOTICS.md#015",
      "path": [
