        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "01 - Antibiotics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nTrue IgE-mediated (anaphylaxis): <1% of penicillin exposures\n  RAST/skin testing available for clarification\n  Major determinant: BPO (benzylpenicilloyl) in skin test\n  Cross-reactivity with cephalosporins: side-chain similarity matters; ~1–2%\n  Cross-reactivity with carbapenems: ~1%\n  Cross-reactivity with aztreonam: NO cross-reactivity with penicillin\n    Exception: aztreonam shares R1 side chain with ceftazidime → cross-reacts with that"
    },
    {
      "id": "01-ANTIBIOTICS.md#023",
      "path": [
        "01-ANTIBIOTICS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:medicine:01-antibiotics, git-history:medicine:01-antibiotics]",
        "canonical_path": "medicine/01-ANTIBIOTICS.md",
        "concepts": "[antibiotics]",
        "current_path": "medicine/01-ANTIBIOTICS.md",
        "id": "maxim:medicine:antibiotics",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "medicine",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[antibiotics]",
        "section": "medicine",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "01 - Antibiotics",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "\"Penicillin allergy\" label causes massive overuse of vancomycin and fluoroquinolones\n→ Drives resistance; allergy delabeling programs important (skin testing/graded challenge)\n```"
    },
